ter semantics are preserved.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["push.py _push_mode L62-63: `return normalize_push_mode(load_config(root=root).sync.push)` re-reads config (env-fed REBAR_SYNC_PUSH) at push time","import_ndjson.py L216-217: `_prev_push = os.environ.get('REBAR_SYNC_PUSH'); os.environ['REBAR_SYNC_PUSH'] = 'off'` — comment: 'Defer push... Restored in finally; the final push then honors the caller's real sync.push policy'","import_ndjson.py L397-401 final push calls push.push_tickets_branch(tracker) AFTER the env restore, relying on push.py reading the (now-restored) policy","config_ownership_exceptions.py rows: push.py load_config is a listed cut (treatment a), REBAR_SYNC_PUSH is the kept owned-in-place read"],"finding":"The plan cuts push.py L63 load_config (treatment a) to thread sync.push from an owned resolver, but keeps import_ndjson.py's REBAR_SYNC_PUSH env write as owned-in-place — these two treatments are coupled: the import sets os.environ['REBAR_SYNC_PUSH']='off' precisely so interior writes' push.py policy (which re-reads config live via load_config) resolves to 'off' and defers per-event pushes. If push.py's policy is resolved once at a composition root before the import runs, the env mutation becomes dead and interior pushes are no longer deferred.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd0c10129f8cd9412","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Decision rule (a) + owned-in-place allowlist item 3; plan step 1; push.py L63 vs import_ndjson.py L216/L217","norm_id":"n3de201a2adcce786","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A bulk `import_tickets` run under REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always: if push.py's policy is snapshotted before import, every interior write pushes (one network round-trip per event) instead of the intended single deferred push"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Either keep push.py's policy resolution l